  "Question": "A triangle has angles of \\(30^\\circ\\) and \\(45^\\circ.\\) If the side opposite the \\(45^\\circ\\) angle has length \\(8,\\) then the side opposite the \\(30^\\circ\\) angle has length:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(4\\)",
    "B": "\\(4\\sqrt2\\)",
    "C": "\\(4\\sqrt3\\)",
    "D": "\\(4\\sqrt6\\)",
    "E": "\\(6\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Name the triangle \\(ABC\\) so that \\(\\angle A=30^\\circ\\), \\(\\angle B=45^\\circ\\), and \\(AC=8\\). The desired side is \\(BC\\). Draw the perpendicular \\(CD\\) from \\(C\\) to \\(AB\\). Since both base angles are acute, \\(D\\) lies between \\(A\\) and \\(B\\).\n\nThis construction puts the known side and the desired side into two right triangles sharing the altitude. In right triangle \\(ACD\\), the side opposite \\(30^\\circ\\) is half the hypotenuse, so\n\\[\nCD=\\frac{AC}{2}=4.\n\\]\nIn right triangle \\(BCD\\), the other acute angle is also \\(45^\\circ\\). Equal angles have equal opposite sides, so \\(BD=CD=4\\). The Pythagorean theorem now gives\n\\[\nBC=\\sqrt{4^2+4^2}=\\sqrt{32}=4\\sqrt2.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(4\\sqrt2\\), choice B.",
